{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head b22b9ae67881bc9cd71ca0f76d0febc29fea480a, resting on all 32 submitted artifacts, packages/log/README.md first.\n\nBoth findings in 07d3150e are substantially addressed. The checked timestamp decoder rejects invalid entry, invitation, delegation, genesis, onboarding and checkpoint times; roster replay also rejects non-finite admission time. Each inspected commit's retained digests and needed evidence are checked. Amendment 2's lane L edits are present: recomputed and land decisions replay with the active policy, checker configurations are retained and checked against accepted checks, onboarding signatures bind the named operator, repository and first admin, and cannotProve identifies the explicit state-proof limits. The five ea4a9bd0 fixes remain intact. One new cache collision leaves malformed retained input approved.\n\nP2 — distinguish retained-file decoding by directory/type as well as digest (packages/log/src/verify.ts, retained-file loop around lines 288–308). The guard skips a file whenever inputs, policyFiles or malformed already has its digest. The same bytes have different contracts under inputs/ and policies/. I first published a valid genesis/activation with DEMO_POLICY under policies/; verification succeeded. In an advancing child I added the exact same bytes at inputs/\u003ctheir-correct-digest\u003e.json. decodeRetained(\"input\", bytes) throws because a policy document is not a replay context, but verifyLog reports ok:true, commits:2, verifiedThrough:2, failures:[]. The earlier policy cache suppresses the input decoder. Publishing the same malformed input in a single root commit produces a malformed failure, so the verdict also depends on which commit first introduced the bytes. This bypasses the promised decoding of every inspected retained input; it does not involve a digest collision or changing signed entry bytes.\n\nCache successful and failed decodes by the decoding contract plus digest (or keep independent input and policy/checker stores without cross-store skip). Preserve per-commit path availability checks and report malformed retained input at each commit that publishes it. Do not let one directory's valid representation suppress another directory's error or poison its valid decode. Add the two-commit policy-to-input case and the reverse-order cases; retain valid shared-byte storage and repeated identical content as positive cases where their respective decoding contracts permit them.\n\nArchitecture: the commit-specific availability checks now preserve historical failures and the owned publication cohort remains sound. Digest equality establishes byte identity, not semantic identity across input, policy and checker decoding. Room recovery still must retain and retry the exact publication cohort and prove its expected commit/parent, as recorded in lane A review 8faa2ef9.\n\nSecurity: invalid timestamps no longer bypass expiry and the new onboarding/checker checks match the approved contract. The remaining defect falsely approves malformed audit evidence when valid bytes were cached under another directory. Local signed fixtures demonstrate the result on Node and workerd; no live repository or credential was used. The grant-time interpretation of delegated \"*\" remains appropriate under R-LOG-10 and still needs the Room to agree.\n\nSimplification: keep one decoding boundary and reuse byte/digest checks, while caching typed decoding separately. Do not repeat policy evaluation merely to validate each commit's retained-file availability.\n\nValidation: clean dependency install; root workspace typecheck passed; unmodified log tests 91/91 Node and 86/86 workerd passed. Two independent diagnostic tests confirmed the cache false approval and the single-commit rejection on both hosts, 2/2 each. All 32 artifact paths were compared to the previous reviewed head: 20 unchanged blobs (including package-lock.json) and all 12 changed/new files reviewed. Diagnostics exist only in /tmp/artroom-checker-log-v3/packages/log/test/checker-v3-review.test.ts; candidate source was not changed. No live round-trip driver was executed.\n\nScope: full state re-derivation remains explicitly open in approved R-LOG-15; this review does not invent or claim that proof. Schedule estimates do not reduce the remaining implementation and integration obligations.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:005a889d8e6bb7de224bb5bb45faa41aacd29423","binding":"assigned","head":"b22b9ae67881bc9cd71ca0f76d0febc29fea480a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c1b3ee12f3049580ee00f16d17d221aa65aaf9b8\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:26f088c3bc7090e81699ffd310739a4424989b87\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4afc032b3879a0fa3cd351c8dc1cf7cfcd622765","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}